{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790697456,"nonce":"e29Wi1O+wxfv4fuyfPjN8oInTUk=","title":"Defer xgpu plugin carrier symbols in the macOS GPU cdylib","message":"The macOS Tests workflow fails while linking librayzor_gpu.dylib for `cargo test -p compiler --lib`. xgpu's generated Rayzor adapter calls host-owned `rayzor_plugin_string_*`, `rayzor_plugin_bytes_*`, `rayzor_plugin_future_*`, and `rayzor_plugin_raise` symbols. Linux permits those unresolved cdylib references for resolution by the host at load time, while Darwin rejects them unless the cdylib opts into dynamic lookup.\n\nReproducer:\n\n    cargo test -p compiler --lib --no-run\n\nThe GPU build script should apply Darwin's `-undefined dynamic_lookup` policy to the cdylib, matching the existing Rayzor tensor and Nue plugin contract without applying the option to ordinary binaries or test harnesses.","files":null}]}